# Metal-oxide gas-sensor resistance across a hotplate sweep -- the VOC signal of
# M01 spec 6.4. Supersedes 1.0, which carried a single setpoint.
#
# MAJOR bump, not the minor one 1.0 anticipated. Types sharing a major version
# must share an extent, and 1.0's 32 bytes cannot hold a ten-element sweep at
# any array capacity -- the reserved capacity, not the length actually sent,
# sets the extent. A minor version was never available for this shape.
#
# Deliberately NOT an air-quality index. IAQ, CO2-equivalent, bVOC-equivalent
# and gas-scan classification are outputs of Bosch's closed-source BSEC, which
# is incompatible with the AGPL reference firmware (ADR-0002 d5), so this
# subject carries raw sensor-API resistances and nothing derived from them. CO2
# is measured by the SCD41 on its own subject, never estimated from this one.
#
# Why a sweep. One resistance at one temperature is a scalar whose absolute
# value means nothing; the same air read 161 kOhm at a 1 s scan interval and
# 18 kOhm at 10 s (spec 6.4). R(T) across several setpoints is a shape, and a
# shape survives the baseline drift a single point does not -- different
# analytes separate by where in temperature they respond, which is the
# discrimination a scalar cannot offer at any baseline.
#
# The sweep is taken as consecutive forced-mode conversions, one per setpoint,
# NOT in the BME688's parallel mode. That is what lets the approved BME680
# alternative of spec 4.2 produce the same vector: forced mode and per-shot
# heater setpoints exist on both parts, so variant_id stays off the critical
# path of every population (spec O-49). It also means the plate cools between
# steps, so each point starts from the same state rather than from its
# predecessor's heat.
#
# Comparability. A reading is comparable only against readings taken with the
# SAME setpoint list AND the same scan interval; both belong to the baseline,
# not just the setpoints. Consumers shall compare index-by-index against
# heater_celsius rather than assuming a fixed list.
uavcan.time.SynchronizedTimestamp.1.0 timestamp
uint16[<=10] heater_celsius   # hotplate targets, ascending, one per sweep step
float32[<=10] ohm             # plate resistance at heater_celsius of the same index
bool valid                    # EVERY step completed and reached heater stability
@extent 96 * 8
